./ R 00643000 00645000 $ 00643100 100                                           
*  WAS SSK R3,R8 / SRL R3,8 / SSK R3,R6 -- THE 2ND HALF        XA0038DK         
*  PAGE'S KEY THEN THE 1ST. AN ESA/390 KEY COVERS THE WHOLE 4  XA0038DK         
*  KB PAGE, SO THE PAIR BECOMES ONE SSKE AND THE SHIFT         XA0038DK         
*  BETWEEN THEM IS NOW THE SELECTION OF WHICH KEY SURVIVES.    XA0038DK         
*  SWPKEY1 IS KEPT, THE FIRST HALF'S. A GUEST THAT SET ITS     XA0038DK         
*  TWO HALVES DIFFERENTLY CANNOT BE REPRESENTED AT ALL --      XA0038DK         
*  THAT IS R-12, GUEST-VISIBLE THROUGH ISKE, AND BELONGS WITH  XA0038DK         
*  M4. RECORDED HERE SO THE CHOICE IS NOT MISTAKEN FOR AN      XA0038DK         
*  EQUIVALENCE. R8 STILL CARRIES THE 2ND-HALF ADDRESS FROM     XA0038DK         
*  00640000 AND IS NOW UNUSED; THE LA IS LEFT ALONE SO NO      XA0038DK         
*  OTHER REGISTER STATE CHANGES. I-177.                        XA0038DK         
         SRL   R3,8           SWPKEY1, THE FIRST HALF'S KEY    XA0038DK         
         SSKE  R3,R6          ONE KEY FOR THE WHOLE PAGE       XA0038DK         
./ R 00939000 00940000 $ 00939100 100                                           
*  WAS SSK R6,R7 / SSK R6,R5 -- FIRST 2K THEN SECOND 2K, BOTH  XA0038DK         
*  WITH THE KEY ZEROED BY SR R6,R6 AT 00937000. ONE KEY, ONE   XA0038DK         
*  INSTRUCTION, AND NOTHING IS LOST BECAUSE BOTH HALVES WERE   XA0038DK         
*  ALREADY BEING SET THE SAME. I-177.                          XA0038DK         
         SSKE  R6,R7          ZERO KEY, WHOLE 4 KB PAGE        XA0038DK         
./ R 01012000          $ 01012100 100                                           
*  ISK PAIR, READ. THE LA R14,2048(,R6) BETWEEN THEM STILL     XA0038DK         
*  NAMES THIS PAGE, SO BOTH ISKES RETURN ITS ONE KEY AND       XA0038DK         
*  01016000'S SWPREF2*256+SWPREF2 MASK FINDS IT IN BOTH        XA0038DK         
*  BYTES. I-192.                                               XA0038DK         
         ISKE  R15,R6         GET STORAGE KEY                  XA0038DK         
./ R 01015000          $ 01015100 100                                           
         ISKE  R15,R14        GET OTHER STORAGE KEY            XA0038DK         
./ R 01021000 01026000 $ 01021100 100                                           
*  WAS RRB 0(R6) / BZ *+8 / OI SWPKEY1,4 / RRB 2048(R6) / BZ   XA0038DK         
*  *+8 / OI SWPKEY2,4. ONE KEY, SO ONE RRBE, AND ITS RESULT    XA0038DK         
*  GOES TO BOTH BACK-UP KEYS. THE BZ NOW HAS TWO OIS TO SKIP   XA0038DK         
*  INSTEAD OF ONE, SO *+8 BECOMES THE LABEL NOBKUP1 RATHER     XA0038DK         
*  THAN *+12 -- R-26. I-192.                                   XA0038DK         
         RRBE  0,R6           ONE KEY FOR THE WHOLE PAGE       XA0038DK         
         BZ    NOBKUP1        NO BITS TO BACK UP               XA0038DK         
         OI    SWPKEY1,4      VIRT. BACK-UP KEY                XA0038DK         
         OI    SWPKEY2,4      BOTH HALVES, ONE REAL KEY        XA0038DK         
NOBKUP1  DS    0H                                              XA0038DK         
./ R 01302000 01308000 $ 01302100 100                                           
*  WAS RRB 0(R6) / BC 8+4,TSTRRB2 / OI SWPKEY1,4 / RRB         XA0038DK         
*  2048(R6) / BC 8+4,STKEY2+4 / STKEY2 DS 0H / OI SWPKEY2,4.   XA0038DK         
*  THE SECOND RRB AND ITS BC GO; THE FALL-THROUGH NOW BACKS    XA0038DK         
*  UP BOTH HALVES FROM THE ONE RESULT. STKEY2 MOVES ONTO THE   XA0038DK         
*  OI SO STKEY2+4 STILL NAMES THE NI AT 01309000, WHICH        XA0038DK         
*  01323000 BRANCHES TO. I-192.                                XA0038DK         
         RRBE  0,R6           ONE KEY FOR THE WHOLE PAGE       XA0038DK         
         BC    8+4,TSTRRB2    REF OFF, PAGE IS A CANDIDATE     XA0038DK         
         OI    SWPKEY1,4      REF. BIT TO VIRT. BACK-UP KEY    XA0038DK         
STKEY2   OI    SWPKEY2,4      AND THE SECOND HALF, ONE KEY     XA0038DK         
./ R 01318000 01321000 $ 01318100 100                                           
*  WAS BALR R14,0 / RRB 2048(R6) / BC 2+1,STKEY2 / BALR        XA0038DK         
*  R15,R0. THE RRB READ THE SECOND HALF'S REFERENCE BIT AND    XA0038DK         
*  THE BC ACTED ON IT; WITH ONE KEY THE BRANCH THAT REACHED    XA0038DK         
*  HERE ALREADY PROVED IT OFF, SO NEITHER CAN FIRE. BOTH       XA0038DK         
*  BALRS STAY AND NOW PARK THE SAME CONDITION CODE, WHICH IS   XA0038DK         
*  WHAT OR R14,R15 COMBINES. I-192.                            XA0038DK         
         IPM   R14            SAVE C.C. FOR CHANGE TEST I-228  XA0038DK         
         IPM   R15            ONE KEY, SO THE SAME C.C.        XA0038DK         
./ R 01461000 01466000 $ 01461100 100                                           
*  BCHNGE. WAS RRB 0(R6) / BC 8+2,*+8 / OI SWPKEY1,2 / RRB     XA0038DK         
*  2048(R6) / BC 8+2,*+8 / OI SWPKEY2,2 -- WHICH OF THE TWO    XA0038DK         
*  KEYS WAS CHANGED. THERE IS ONE, AND ITS CHANGE BIT APPLIES  XA0038DK         
*  TO BOTH HALVES. THE *+8 BECOMES NOCHGBK, R-26. I-192.       XA0038DK         
         RRBE  0,R6           ONE KEY FOR THE WHOLE PAGE       XA0038DK         
         BC    8+2,NOCHGBK    NOT CHANGED                      XA0038DK         
         OI    SWPKEY1,2      BACK-UP CHANGE BITS              XA0038DK         
         OI    SWPKEY2,2      BOTH HALVES, ONE REAL KEY        XA0038DK         
NOCHGBK  DS    0H                                              XA0038DK         
./ R 01987000 01994000 $ 01987100 100                                           
*  WAS RRB 0(R1) / BALR R14,0 / BC 8+4,*+8 / OI SWPKEY1,4 /    XA0038DK         
*  RRB 2048(R1) / BALR R15,0 / BC 8+4,*+8 / OI SWPKEY2,4.      XA0038DK         
*  BOTH BALRS STAY AND PARK THE SAME CONDITION CODE, WHICH IS  XA0038DK         
*  WHAT OR R14,R15 AT 01998000 COMBINES AND SPM R14 AT         XA0038DK         
*  02001000 RESTORES. THE TWO *+8 OFFSETS BECOME ONE LABEL,    XA0038DK         
*  NOREFBK, R-26. I-192.                                       XA0038DK         
         RRBE  0,R1           ONE KEY FOR THE WHOLE PAGE       XA0038DK         
         IPM   R14            SAVE CONDITION CODE, I-228       XA0038DK         
         IPM   R15            ONE KEY, SO THE SAME C.C.        XA0038DK         
         BC    8+4,NOREFBK    REF WAS OFF, NOTHING TO BACK UP  XA0038DK         
         OI    SWPKEY1,4      REF. BIT RESET, BACK-UP TO VIRT  XA0038DK         
         OI    SWPKEY2,4      BOTH HALVES, ONE REAL KEY        XA0038DK         
NOREFBK  DS    0H                                              XA0038DK         
